+# Pre-ship review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Scope: `packages/nextjs` frontend and its configuration, plus the contract
+address/config it depends on. Reviewed against the repo's own `AGENTS.md`
+conventions. Verified by reading the code, running `yarn check-types`,
+`yarn lint`, `next build`, and querying Base mainnet directly.
+
+Report only — no code was changed.
+
+**Verdict: do not ship.** Issue 1 alone means every payout attempt reverts,
+and issue 2 means the payout feed never renders.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. No contract is deployed at the Payouts address on Base
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:10`
+
+`Payouts.address` is `0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`. `eth_getCode`
+for that address on Base mainnet returns `0x` from two independent RPCs
+(`https://mainnet.base.org` and `https://base-rpc.publicnode.com`) — there is no
+code there. For contrast, the USDC address in the same file
+(`0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`) does return bytecode, so the RPCs
+and the query are fine; the Payouts address is the problem.
+
+Corroborating: `packages/hardhat/deployments/` does not exist, so
+`00_deploy_payouts.ts` has never produced a recorded Base deployment. The
+`deployedOnBlock: 33712450` and the address look like hand-written placeholders
+in a file whose header says "autogenerated … do not edit manually".
+
+Impact: every `pay()` call reverts (call to an address with no code), and
+`approve()` silently grants a USDC allowance to a dead address. Users see
+nothing but a failed transaction — see issue 4.
+
+**Fix:** actually deploy — `yarn deploy --network base --tags Payouts` — and let
+the deploy pipeline regenerate `deployedContracts.ts` with the real address and
+deployment block. Do not hand-edit the address. Before shipping, re-verify with
+`cast code <address> --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org` (or the `eth_getCode`
+call above) that the address has bytecode.
+
+### 2. The payout feed scans Base from block 0
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:29-34`
+
+```ts
+const { data: payouts } = useScaffoldEventHistory({
+  contractName: "Payouts",
+  eventName: "Paid",
+  fromBlock: 0n,
+  watch: true,
+});
+```
+
+`useScaffoldEventHistory` pages through history in `blocksBatchSize` chunks of
+500 blocks, one `eth_getLogs` per page, fired sequentially from a `useEffect`
+(`hooks/scaffold-eth/useScaffoldEventHistory.ts:95,257-267`). Base head is
+currently ~51.7M. From block 0 that is **~103,000 sequential RPC round-trips**
+before the first payout ever renders. In practice the list stays empty forever
+and the app rate-limits itself (and the shared Alchemy key — issue 6) off the RPC.
+
+Two aggravating factors:
+
+- The explicit `fromBlock: 0n` is what causes this. The hook already defaults to
+  the contract's `deployedOnBlock` when `fromBlock` is omitted
+  (`useScaffoldEventHistory.ts:128-135`).
+- The feed is rendered *outside* the `isConnected` gate (`page.tsx:118-131`), so
+  the scan starts for every anonymous visitor who lands on the page.
+
+Also note the hook is explicitly `@deprecated` for non-local chains
+(`useScaffoldEventHistory.ts:57-61`): "It uses getLogs which can overload RPC
+endpoints (especially on L2s)."
+
+**Fix (minimum to ship):** delete the `fromBlock: 0n` line so the hook starts at
+the real `deployedOnBlock`, and gate the query on the page being useful, e.g.
+`enabled: isConnected`. **Fix (right answer for a production L2 app):** index
+`Paid` events with Ponder (`.agents/skills/ponder/SKILL.md`) or a subgraph and
+query that, per the hook's own deprecation notice.
+
+### 3. Raw wagmi `useWriteContract` instead of `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6,21,38-43,51-56`
+
+The page calls wagmi's `useWriteContract` directly with hand-passed
+`address`/`abi`. `AGENTS.md` mandates the scaffold hooks, and this is not a style
+nit — `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+(`hooks/scaffold-eth/useScaffoldWriteContract.ts:87-140`) provides four things
+this page loses:
+
+- **Wrong-network guard** (lines 98-106). As written, wagmi broadcasts to
+  whatever chain the wallet happens to be on. A user connected to Ethereum
+  mainnet signs an `approve` against `0x8335…2913` on *mainnet* — a different
+  contract entirely — with no warning. The page never checks `chainId` and never
+  passes one to `writeContractAsync`.
+- **Pre-flight simulation** with a decoded revert reason (lines 118-124).
+- **`useTransactor`** (line 138): the pending/success/error toasts and the
+  *wait for the receipt* step.
+- **`isMining`**, which stays true until the tx is mined. The page's `isPending`
+  (line 21) clears the moment the wallet returns a hash. The "Send Payout" button
+  re-enables while the payout is still in the mempool, with no success feedback
+  anywhere — a user who sees nothing happen clicks again and sends the payout
+  twice. This is a real-money double-send.
+
+**Fix:** replace with two scaffold hooks and use `isMining` for the disabled state:
+
+```ts
+const { writeContractAsync: writeUsdc, isMining: isApproving } =
+  useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "USDC" });
+const { writeContractAsync: writePayouts, isMining: isPaying } =
+  useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" });
+
+await writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parsedAmount, memo] });
+```
+
+Disable Approve on `isApproving` and Send Payout on `isPaying` — separately (see
+issue 13).
+
+### 4. Every failure is swallowed into `console.error`
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46,59-61`
+
+```ts
+} catch (e) {
+  console.error(e);
+}
+```
+
+User rejection, insufficient allowance, insufficient balance, a reverting
+contract (issue 1), a bad address (issue 5) — all of them produce an identical
+result on screen: nothing. The form doesn't clear, no toast, no inline error. For
+a page that moves money, a payout that silently does nothing is the worst
+possible failure mode, and it's the *default* mode today given issue 1.
+
+`AGENTS.md` is explicit: "Use `notification` from `~~/utils/scaffold-eth` for
+success/error/warning feedback and `getParsedError` for readable error messages."
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```ts
+import { getParsedError, notification } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+} catch (e) {
+  notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+}
+```
+
+Adopting `useScaffoldWriteContract` (issue 3) also brings the success and
+pending toasts via `useTransactor`, so the two fixes are complementary.
+
+### 5. Recipient address is never validated
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84,55`
+
+`recipient` is a free-text `<input type="text">` blind-cast at the call site:
+`args: [recipient as `0x${string}`, …]`. The cast is a lie to the compiler —
+nothing checks the string. Empty, truncated, or mistyped input throws inside
+viem's encoder and lands in the silent `catch` from issue 4. A checksum-invalid
+address is rejected; an *incorrectly typed but well-formed* address is not, and
+the funds are gone.
+
+**Fix:** use SE-2's `AddressInput` from `@scaffold-ui/components` per
+`AGENTS.md`'s UI Components section — it validates and resolves ENS:
+
+```tsx
+<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="Recipient address" />
+```
+
+and guard the handler with viem's `isAddress(recipient)`, disabling "Send Payout"
+until it passes. For a payouts app also consider an explicit confirm step showing
+the resolved recipient and amount before signing.
+
+### 6. Production ships Scaffold-ETH's shared default API keys
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:16,29,40`
+
+```ts
+export const DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY = "IZYEU2cWBgnFmgiTAgpWD";
+// ...
+walletConnectProjectId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID || '3a8170812b534d0ff9d794f19a901d64',
+```
+
+Neither env var is set anywhere in the repo (`.env.example` has both blank, no
+`.env.local` exists), so a Vercel deploy without dashboard env vars falls back to
+the public SE-2 demo keys. Two distinct consequences:
+
+- **WalletConnect project IDs are origin-allowlisted.** The shared demo ID does
+  not allowlist your production domain, so WalletConnect (and therefore most
+  mobile wallets) will fail to connect for real users.
+- The shared Alchemy key is a public prototyping key with no rate-limit headroom
+  for a live app — and it's the *fallback* transport for Base
+  (`services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20`).
+
+**Fix:** create your own Alchemy app and WalletConnect project, set
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` in the
+Vercel project's environment (all environments), allowlist the production domain
+in the WalletConnect dashboard, and verify the deployed bundle isn't using the
+defaults before launch.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 7. `USDC` was hand-added to the autogenerated `deployedContracts.ts`
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50` (and header, lines 1-4)
+
+The file says "This file is autogenerated by Scaffold-ETH. You should not edit it
+manually or your changes might be overwritten." The `USDC` entry is not produced
+by `packages/hardhat/deploy/00_deploy_payouts.ts`, which only deploys `Payouts`.
+The next `yarn deploy` regenerates this file and drops `USDC`, breaking the
+balance read and the approve flow. Meanwhile `contracts/externalContracts.ts` —
+the file that exists precisely for this — is empty.
+
+**Fix:** move the `USDC` block (address + ABI) into `externalContracts.ts` under
+key `8453`. Both files feed the same `ContractName` union, so
+`useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC" })` keeps working unchanged.
+
+### 8. 30-second polling interval on an L2
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`
+
+`pollingInterval: 30000` against Base, which produces a block every ~2s.
+`AGENTS.md` says "Remember to decrease the polling interval for L2 chains."
+`useScaffoldReadContract` invalidates on `useBlockNumber`
+(`useScaffoldReadContract.ts:64-77`), so the displayed USDC balance can lag a
+completed payout by half a minute — which, combined with the missing success
+toast (issue 3), makes a successful payout indistinguishable from a failed one.
+
+**Fix:** drop to `pollingInterval: 2000` (or a few seconds) to match Base block
+time.
+
+### 9. No allowance check — the approve/pay flow is guesswork
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62,99-114`
+
+Two always-enabled buttons, no indication of which is needed. Concretely:
+
+- A returning user with a sufficient allowance pays for a redundant `approve`.
+- A user who skips `approve` gets a revert with no message (issue 4).
+- `handleApprove` approves *exactly* the amount in the box at click time. Edit
+  the amount upward before clicking Send Payout and the payout reverts —
+  silently, again.
+
+The USDC ABI already includes `allowance` (`deployedContracts.ts:78`), so the
+data is one hook away.
+
+**Fix:** read the allowance and drive the UI from it:
+
+```ts
+const { data: allowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+  functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, PAYOUTS_ADDRESS],
+});
+const needsApproval = (allowance ?? 0n) < parsedAmount;
+```
+
+Show only Approve when `needsApproval`, only Send Payout otherwise. Also block
+submission when `parsedAmount > usdcBalance` with an inline "insufficient
+balance" message.
+
+### 10. Contract address and ABI hardcoded by chain ID
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:10-11`
+
+```ts
+const PAYOUTS = deployedContracts[8453].Payouts;
+const USDC = deployedContracts[8453].USDC;
+```
+
+This bypasses `useDeployedContractInfo` / `useTargetNetwork` and hardcodes Base's
+chain ID at module scope. Adding Base Sepolia to `targetNetworks` for staging —
+or any multi-network work — silently keeps pointing at mainnet. It's also what
+makes issue 3 possible, since the raw address/ABI are what get handed to wagmi.
+
+**Fix:** falls out of fixing issue 3 — the scaffold hooks resolve address and ABI
+from the selected network. If you need the address directly (e.g. for the
+allowance spender in issue 9), get it from
+`useDeployedContractInfo({ contractName: "Payouts" })`.
+
+### 11. Hardcoded black background breaks theming
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65,121`
+
+`className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white"` and `border-gray-700`. The app
+ships a full DaisyUI light/dark theme (`styles/globals.css`) with a working theme
+switcher in the footer. This page ignores both: in light mode it's a black
+rectangle wedged between a light header and footer. `AGENTS.md`'s styling section
+calls this out directly.
+
+**Fix:** use semantic DaisyUI tokens — `bg-base-100 text-base-content` on the
+wrapper, and make each payout row a `card bg-base-200` (or
+`border border-base-300`) instead of `border-gray-700`.
+
+### 12. Array index used as React key on a live-updating list
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:120-121`
+
+`key={i}` on a list that `watch: true` **prepends** new events to
+(`useScaffoldEventHistory.ts:247`). Every new payout shifts all indices, so React
+re-keys the entire list and rebinds existing rows to different payouts. Stale
+render artifacts on a list of financial transactions.
+
+**Fix:** `key={`${payout.transactionHash}-${payout.logIndex}`}` — the hook's own
+dedupe uses exactly that identity (`useScaffoldEventHistory.ts:276`).
+
+### 13. `btn loading` is DaisyUI 4 syntax; shared pending state
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:100-113`
+
+Two problems in the same block. First, the project is on DaisyUI 5
+(`package.json`: `"daisyui": "5.5.19"`), where `loading` is a standalone
+component class, not a `btn` modifier — applying it to the button doesn't render
+the intended spinner. Second, both buttons share one `isPending`, so approving
+disables Send Payout and vice versa.
+
+**Fix:** track the two mutations separately (issue 3 gives you `isApproving` /
+`isPaying`) and use the DaisyUI 5 pattern:
+
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isApproving} onClick={handleApprove}>
+  {isApproving && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm" />}
+  Approve
+</button>
+```
+
+### 14. Site metadata is still Scaffold-ETH boilerplate
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:10-13`
+
+`title: 'Scaffold-ETH 2 App'`, `description: 'Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2'`, and
+`getMetadata` appends the `"%s | Scaffold-ETH 2"` template
+(`utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8`). The OG image is still
+`public/thumbnail.jpg`, the stock SE-2 thumbnail. Every browser tab, search
+result, and shared link for a real payments product says "Scaffold-ETH 2 App".
+
+**Fix:** set a real title/description in `layout.tsx`, change `titleTemplate` in
+`getMetadata.ts:8`, and replace `public/thumbnail.jpg` and `public/favicon.png`.
+Also update `public/manifest.json`.
+
+### 15. The landing page is untouched SE-2 boilerplate
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx`
+
+`/` still reads "Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2", tells the visitor to "Get started by
+editing packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx" and "Edit your smart contract
+YourContract.sol" (a file that doesn't exist in this repo — the contract is
+`Payouts.sol`), and its two call-to-action cards point at Debug Contracts and the
+Block Explorer. There is no link to `/payouts` anywhere on the page. This is the
+first thing every real user sees.
+
+**Fix:** replace with a short product intro and a primary CTA to `/payouts`.
+
+### 16. Developer-only routes are exposed in production
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx:29-33`; `packages/nextjs/app/blockexplorer/`
+
+"Debug Contracts" sits in the main nav unconditionally, and `/blockexplorer` is
+still a routable page in the production bundle (confirmed in the build output).
+The Footer already hides its explorer link off-localhost
+(`components/Footer.tsx:33-41`) and the explorer page itself just fires an error
+toast on non-local chains (`app/blockexplorer/page.tsx:28-40`) — so a user who
+finds the route gets a raw error toast. Debug also exposes arbitrary write calls
+to the Payouts contract with no guardrails.
+
+**Fix:** gate the Debug nav entry on `targetNetwork.id === hardhat.id` (the
+`isLocalNetwork` value is already computed at `Header.tsx:67` and currently
+unused for this), and delete `app/blockexplorer/` and `app/debug/` from the
+production build, or move them behind the same local-network check.
+
+### 17. The deploy script ignores TypeScript errors
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/package.json:17`
+
+`yarn vercel:yolo`, which `AGENTS.md` names as *the* frontend deploy command,
+passes `NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR=true`; `next.config.ts:7-9` turns that
+into `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors`. Type errors — the exact class of bug that
+would have caught the `recipient as `0x${string}`` cast in issue 5 had it not
+been an explicit cast — cannot fail a production deploy.
+
+`yarn check-types` and `yarn lint` both pass today (lint emits 100 prettier
+warnings, 0 errors — see issue 19), so turning this off costs nothing right now.
+
+**Fix:** deploy with `yarn vercel --prod` instead of `vercel:yolo`, and add
+`yarn check-types` to CI so type regressions block the merge rather than sliding
+into production.
+
+### 18. `next build` fails on Node 25; `engines` permits it
+
+**File:** `package.json:58-60` (root)
+
+Reproduced: with this machine's default Node (v25.9.0), `yarn next build` fails —
+
+```
+Error occurred prerendering page "/_not-found".
+TypeError: localStorage.getItem is not a function
+```
+
+Root cause: RainbowKit 2.2.9 guards its storage reads with
+`typeof localStorage !== "undefined"`
+(`node_modules/@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/dist/index.js:1452,1963,4186`). Node 25
+exposes a global `localStorage` that is present but non-functional unless
+`--localstorage-file` gets a real path, so the guard passes and the call throws
+during prerender. Confirmed both directions: the same build **succeeds** on Node
+v22.23.1, and succeeds on Node 25 with `NODE_OPTIONS=--localstorage-file=/tmp/x.json`.
+
+The root `engines` field says `"node": ">=22.10.0"`, which permits Node 25, so
+whether your build works depends on which Node the build machine happens to pick.
+
+**Fix:** pin the runtime — set `"node": "22.x"` in root `engines`, add a `.nvmrc`
+with `22`, and set the Node version explicitly in the Vercel project settings.
+Longer term, upgrade RainbowKit once a release guards on `typeof window` instead.
+
+### 19. `yarn lint` emits 100 formatting warnings
+
+`yarn lint` reports "100 problems (0 errors, 100 warnings)", all
+`prettier/prettier`, concentrated in the files that were hand-edited for this
+feature — `scaffold.config.ts`, `app/layout.tsx`, `utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts`,
+`services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`. `wagmiConfig.tsx:20` in
+particular is an entire `createClient` factory collapsed onto one ~700-character
+line, which is genuinely hard to review.
+
+Because they're warnings, `yarn build` (which runs `yarn lint && next build`)
+passes anyway, so this only gets worse.
+
+**Fix:** run `yarn format`. Consider promoting `prettier/prettier` to `error` in
+`eslint.config.mjs` so the pre-existing Husky hook actually enforces it.
+
+### 20. No loading state on the balance; misleading zero
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:75`
+
+```tsx
+{usdcBalance !== undefined ? formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6) : "0"}
+```
+
+While the read is in flight, the page asserts the user's balance is **0 USDC** —
+indistinguishable from an actually-empty wallet. With `pollingInterval: 30000`
+(issue 8) that window is not short.
+
+**Fix:** render a skeleton or `loading loading-dots` while `isLoading`, and only
+show a number once data has arrived. Also prefer the `Balance` component from
+`@scaffold-ui/components` where it fits, per `AGENTS.md`.
+
+### 21. Amount input accepts negative and out-of-range values
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:85-91,42,55`
+
+A bare `<input type="number">` with no `min`/`step`. `-5` reaches
+`parseUnits(amount, 6)` as a negative bigint, which throws on uint256 encoding
+and disappears into the silent catch (issue 4). `0` passes the client entirely
+and reverts on-chain against `require(amount > 0)` (`Payouts.sol:22`). More than
+6 decimal places is silently truncated with no warning that the user is sending
+less than they typed.
+
+**Fix:** use `IntegerInput`/`EtherInput` from `@scaffold-ui/components` (per
+`AGENTS.md`) or add `min="0" step="0.01"`, and validate before submit:
+`parsedAmount > 0n && parsedAmount <= (usdcBalance ?? 0n)`, disabling the button
+otherwise.
+
+### 22. Form inputs have no labels
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-97`
+
+Three inputs identified only by `placeholder`. Placeholders vanish on focus and
+are not reliable accessible names, so screen-reader users get three unlabeled
+fields on a form that moves money, and sighted users lose the field identity
+while typing.
+
+**Fix:** wrap each in DaisyUI's `fieldset` / `label` pattern with a real
+`<label htmlFor>` bound to an input `id`.
+
+---
+
+## Verified clean
+
+Worth recording, so these don't get re-litigated:
+
+- `yarn check-types` passes with no errors (fresh, non-incremental run).
+- `yarn lint` reports 0 errors (100 formatting warnings — issue 19).
+- `next build` succeeds on Node 22 and produces all 8 routes (issue 18 is
+  Node-25-specific).
+- The USDC address `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` is the correct
+  canonical Base USDC, and has bytecode on chain. It matches the constant in
+  `packages/hardhat/deploy/00_deploy_payouts.ts`. 6 decimals is right for it, so
+  the hardcoded `6` in `formatUnits`/`parseUnits` is not a bug today — though
+  reading `decimals()` would be more robust.
+- `Payouts.sol` itself is sound for its scope: zero-address and zero-amount
+  guards, checked `transferFrom` return value, no reentrancy surface, `usdc`
+  immutable. The contract is not the problem — the address pointing at it is
+  (issue 1).
+- `burnerWalletMode: 'localNetworksOnly'` correctly keeps the burner wallet out
+  of the Base build (`services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:16-18`).

